## Why This Is Asked
This question tests the ability to design a real-time aggregated leaderboard with sliding windows and per-key deduplication. It combines hash tables, heaps, and lazy expiration techniques to achieve O(log K) top-K retrieval while maintaining constant-time lookups.

## Key Concepts
- **Sliding window by timestamp**: Only events within the last W seconds contribute to the sum
- **Per-city deduplication**: Within each city, only the latest event per (city, driver_id) counts—older events from the same driver are discarded
- **City sums**: Maintained via per-city hashmaps and a max-heap for efficient ranking
- **Global top-K**: Implemented with a min-heap supporting O(log K) retrieval per update

